STEP 0 supports a build, but only on Track B. I’m using a native bounded-treewidth family: two succinctly specified simple graphs, each a prime cycle plus isolated vertices (treewidth 2), related by a planted projective vertex bijection. The paper’s general algorithm can materialize and canonize the graphs in polynomial time; the intended shortcut is to recognize conjugate projective edge generators and return the \(2\times2\) change-of-coordinates matrix. This keeps the witness short while the mechanical graph traversal grows.
