The viable route is Track B, using the paper’s native constrained-isomorphism objects from Section 5 rather than pretending bounded-treewidth GI is hard. I’ll generate colored graphs and a direct-product affine permutation group, plant a group element, and make the short route a power-sum normalization invariant; the reference solver will be exhaustive two-point anchoring in the allowed coset. This preserves exact graph-isomorphism verification while keeping the answer a compact permutation-group element.
