-reported separately, while a solver without tools can compress it only by
-recognizing how centered power sums transform.
+Construction. U=[[1,1],[0,1]] acts on P^1(F_p) as one p-cycle plus its fixed
+point. Sample two projective coordinate systems C1,C2 first, publish
+A=C1*U*C1^-1 and B=C2*U*C2^-1, and retain T=C2*C1^-1. Thus T*A*T^-1=B by
+construction; generation never solves the published instance. Repeating the
+same component and adding isolated vertices changes only graph size and
+isomorphism type, never the certificate. Both public graphs have tree width 2.
 
