+The projective line P^1(F_{p}) has the labels 0,...,{p - 1},inf. A matrix
+M=[[a,b],[c,d]] with nonzero determinant acts as follows:
+  M(x) = (a*x+b)/(c*x+d) for x in F_{p};
+  M(x) = inf when c*x+d=0;
+  M(inf) = a/c when c!=0, and M(inf)=inf when c=0.
+Division means multiplication by the unique modular inverse.
 
+For such a matrix M, define the finite undirected simple graph G(M). Its
+vertices are the projective labels plus I_0,...,I_{inst['isolated_count'] - 1}, where every I_j is
+isolated. For each projective label x with M(x)!=x, G(M) has the unordered edge
+{{x,M(x)}}; repeated descriptions of the same edge count only once. The two
+matrices below each generate one cycle of length {p} and one fixed projective
+vertex, so each graph has tree width 2.
 
