-(arXiv:1803.06858).  Each instance consists of two exactly represented colored
-graphs and an allowed direct product of affine permutation groups.  A planted
-group element is sampled before the second graph is constructed.
+Each matrix below acts on the projective line over a prime field.  Its orbit
+edges form one p-cycle and one isolated vertex, hence a graph of tree width 2.
+Two independently relabelled copies are made isomorphic by a projective change
+of coordinates sampled before either public edge generator is formed.
 
-Only the Python standard library is required.  Importing this module performs
-no file I/O, network access, or printing.
