-the algorithm actually computes the complete isomorphism coset.  This is an
-honest Track-B family: the standard allowed-group search succeeds and is
-reported separately, while a solver without tools can compress it only by
-recognizing how centered power sums transform.
+Construction. U=[[1,1],[0,1]] acts on P^1(F_p) as one p-cycle plus its fixed
+point. Sample two projective coordinate systems C1,C2 first, publish
+A=C1*U*C1^-1 and B=C2*U*C2^-1, and retain T=C2*C1^-1. Thus T*A*T^-1=B by
+construction; generation never solves the published instance. Repeating the
+same component and adding isolated vertices changes only graph size and
+isomorphism type, never the certificate. Both public graphs have tree width 2.
 
-Generation. For each color, make_instance samples a nonzero affine multiplier,
-a translation, and a uniform support set S before forming T=aS+b.  The colored
-graph has all edges inside each support set and no other edges, so its tree
-width is support_size-1.  The sampled affine maps are therefore isomorphisms by
-construction.  They are never recovered by solving a generated instance.
-Raw first, second, and third power sums are included as exact redundant graph
-checksums.  Nonzero centered second and third sums are enforced while sampling
-so that their covariant normalization is always defined.
+Mechanical and compact routes. The reference route treats the descriptions as
+graphs: materialize every successor, locate the isolated fixed point, traverse
+a whole cycle, and check the induced bijection. Its operation and wall-clock
+cost are measured at the shipping preset. The compact route notices that A and
+B are conjugate parabolic projectivities, obtains their double fixed points,
+and fits the unique projectivity through three corresponding points. It is
+also executed in selftest and its exact-operation counter must stay below 300.
 
-Easy regimes and attacks. Unrestricted isomorphism of these clique-plus-
