-the algorithm actually computes the complete isomorphism coset.  This is an
-honest Track-B family: the standard allowed-group search succeeds and is
-reported separately, while a solver without tools can compress it only by
-recognizing how centered power sums transform.
+Construction. U=[[1,1],[0,1]] acts on P^1(F_p) as one p-cycle plus its fixed
+point. Use that point as a hub adjacent to the cycle and to pendant leaves.
+Sample two projective coordinate systems C1,C2 first, publish
+A=C1*U*C1^-1 and B=C2*U*C2^-1, and retain T=C2*C1^-1. Thus T*A*T^-1=B by
+construction; generation never solves the published instance. Changing the
+number of pendant leaves changes graph size and isomorphism type, never the
+certificate. Both public graphs are connected and have tree width 3.
 
-Generation. For each color, make_instance samples a nonzero affine multiplier,
