+phi(u)phi(v) in E(G'). Definition 3 fixes tree decompositions and tree width.
+Theorem 1 rules out Track A: it tests isomorphism in
+2^(k polylog k) poly(N). Theorem 2 also canonizes in
+2^O(k^2 log k) poly(N), and Theorem 15 in Section 6 explicitly computes the
+isomorphism coset. These are the decisive easy results and the certificate
+algorithm. At k=3 the family is therefore honestly Track B.
 
