Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s bounded-treewidth graph-isomorphism problem.

Deliverables:

- [gen_1803_06858.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/gen_1803_06858.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The family inverse-generates connected treewidth-3 wheel graphs and supplies a normalized \(2\times2\) projective isomorphism certificate. All nine local gates pass:

- Uniform guesses: 0/200,000
- Exact witness density: \(2/(p^2-1)\)
- Four attacks: 0/8 each
- Reference algorithm: 3,151,396 operations, 3.252 s maximum
- Compact route: 65 operations
