+NOTES = r"""
+STEP 0. Section 2 defines all graphs to be finite, undirected, and simple and
+defines an isomorphism phi by the exact biconditional uv in E(G) iff
+phi(u)phi(v) in E(G'). Definition 3 fixes tree decompositions and tree width.
+Theorem 1 rules out Track A: it tests isomorphism in
+2^(k polylog k) poly(N). Theorem 2 also canonizes in
+2^O(k^2 log k) poly(N), and Theorem 15 in Section 6 explicitly computes the
+isomorphism coset. Section 7 explicitly defines graph isomorphism restricted
+to a supplied permutation group and gives the relevant Luks-style canonical
+labeling machinery. These are the decisive easy results and the certificate
