| hard | 2,147,483,647 | 2,147,483,647 | 4,294,967,295–10,737,418,236 | available escalation |

`escalate()` continues through known larger primes while the matrix remains
writable. Once coefficient digits approach the output limit, it keeps the
prime fixed and multiplies only the pendant-vertex padding, growing the graph
haystack without lengthening the four-entry witness.

