\section{The structure of the automorphism group}\label{sec:aut:group}

  In this section, we study the automorphism groups of graphs of
  bounded tree width. Our first result states that the automorphism
  groups of graphs of tree width at most $k$ can be
  formed from the automorphism groups of $k$-basic graphs of tree width at
  most $k$ by (repeatedly) taking direct products and wreath
  products with a symmetric top group. This underlines once more the central role of
  the $k$-basic graphs, which we already observed in the previous
  sections. 

  Let $\Phi_k$ be the class of all automorphism groups of $k$-basic
  graphs of tree width at most $k$. It follows from the results of the
  previous section that we can put these groups into the class
  $\Gammak$ by fixing a single vertex. % This significantly
  % restrict the class of groups in $\Phi_k$
  % and it is the foundation of our canonization algorithm in the
  % following section. Recall that a group is in $\Gammak$ if all
  % non-Abelian composition factors are subgroups of the symmetric group
  % $\sym(k)$. 
  We prove an even stronger restriction on the non-Abelian
  composition factors of groups in $\Phi_k$: they are $\ZZ_p^2$-free
  for all primes $p>k$. 
It follows that the non-Abelian
  composition factors of automorphism groups of graphs of tree width
  at most $k$ are either alternating groups or $\ZZ_p^2$-free
  for all primes $p>k$. 
% Our goal is to describe the automorphism groups
% of graphs with tree width $k$.

