codex
I found and am fixing an important G4 issue before declaring the local gates final. A solver gets the unique hub correspondence for free from the statement, so sampling from all of \(PGL(2,p)\) was too loose. The structure-aware language must sample only projectivities sending \(G(A)\)’s hub to \(G(B)\)’s hub. That changes the exact guess density from \(2/(p^2-1)\) to \(2/(p-1)\); the previous `easy` shipping preset therefore did not honestly pass G4.

I’m moving the shipping rung to a prime above two million, implementing uniform sampling from the hub-mapping coset, and remeasuring the baseline. This is precisely the kind of correction the structure-aware gate is meant to catch.
