codex
The corrected structure-aware sampler is now exact: for small fields I exhaustively proved it contains exactly \(p(p-1)\) hub-respecting projectivities and \(2p\) valid witnesses; at the new shipping prime \(p=4{,}194{,}301\), the exact density is \(2/(p-1)=4.768\times10^{-7}\), with 0/200,000 sampled hits.

The larger honest shipping rung makes the explicit reference baseline substantial—one measured seed took about 14.3 seconds and 100.8 million counted operations—while the intended route remains a four-entry matrix and 65 field operations. I’m running the complete gate suite now; it should take roughly two minutes because G6 requires eight full reference runs.
