codex
Built a self-contained Track B generator for bounded-treewidth graph isomorphism. Track A would be false because the paper provides FPT isomorphism and canonization algorithms ([arXiv:1803.06858](https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.06858)).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1803_06858.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/gen_1803_06858.py:25)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/README.md:15)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability \(2/4{,}194{,}300\).
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference algorithm: 100,844,171 operations, 14.715 seconds maximum.
- Compact route: 65 operations.
- Answer: 31 characters, four atomic elements.

STEP 4 remains externally blocked: every oracle request received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before producing an answer. The transcripts preserve those failures, but they are not hardness evidence; the README correctly marks this as a shipping candidate, not hardened. After restoring the key quota, rerun:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1803_06858.py
```

Then rerun the two G9 scratch-directory arms described in the README.
