codex
Implemented and locally verified the Track B generator.

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/gen_1803_06858.py:1)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/selftest_report.json:1)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/README.md:1)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.06858/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl:1)

The family inverse-generates isomorphic treewidth-3 projective wheel graphs. The witness is a normalized \(2\times2\) projective matrix, verified exactly through conjugation. Track A is ruled out by the paper’s FPT isomorphism and canonization algorithms. [Full arXiv text](https://arxiv.org/html/1803.06858v1).

All local gates pass at the medium candidate:

- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(2/8{,}388{,}616\).
- Reference route: 209,693,940 operations, 337.539 seconds worst case.
- Compact route: 65 exact field operations.
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Answer: 31 characters, 4 atoms.

Final hardening remains externally blocked. Easy was defeated when one oracle solved it; medium recorded two failures, but the required third attempt and both G9 arms could not run after OpenRouter returned total-limit HTTP 403 on every redraw. The files explicitly mark medium as a candidate, not hardened or shippable.
